From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:31:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda tests: shared-prefix copy, compact before
 evict and the kept cap with the host RAM tier (MiaAI-Lab recipe patches 0071,
 0074, 0077)

The host RAM tier (TF_GLM_KEPT_HOST, TF_GLM_HOST_CACHE_GIB: kept_host) parks only the kept prompts that rank 0 evicts,
for room or when a request takes their extent over; the kept cap's drops (TF_GLM_CACHE_ENTRIES) go without parking.
The recipe's patches 0071, 0074 and 0077 change which kept prompts are evicted or dropped, so these tests run them with
the tier on the AFD attention node's decoder (world 1 over the fake AFD wire, every reply checked against the request
served alone):

- 0071 (TF_GLM_SHARED_PREFIX_COPY): unset, a sub-agent resuming the writer's system block takes the writer's extent
  over and evicts the writer's own state, which parks and comes back from host RAM at the writer's next turn; set,
  the shared rows are copied, nothing parks, and the next turn resumes on the GPU. The same cached count either way.
- 0074 (TF_GLM_COMPACT_BEFORE_EVICT), TF_GLM_CACHE_ROOM unset: a prompt that needs rows the free rows hold in pieces
  evicts and parks the two oldest kept prompts unset, none set (the extents move together); the oldest prompt's next
  turn resumes from host RAM or from the GPU. With TF_GLM_CACHE_ROOM=1, 0074 changes nothing: the same kept prompts,
  extents, parks and cached counts.
- 0077 (TF_GLM_CAP_SHARED_RECENCY): past the cap the run's system-block state goes unset and stays set; no state the
  cap drops parks, so the agent's next run resumes the system block only with 0077 (and its takeover of the first
  run's extent, without 0071, parks the first run's own state).

Tests: tests/test_glm_recipe_host_tier.py (9, CPU).

Credit: patches 0071 and 0074 were written by ezoushen (https://github.com/ezoushen) and patch 0077 by MiaAI-Lab
